My decision is made.
I am going to take this shirt.
I step away from the mirror.
I smile and turn to the shopkeeper.
"Dada, pack this very shirt," I tell him.
"Certainly, Madam," he says warmly.
"You liked the shirt, right?"
"Yes, I liked it a lot," I say.
I place the new shirt on the counter.
He puts the new shirt in a bag.
He gives the bag to me.
"Thank you for exchanging the shirt, Dada," I say.
"No problem, Madam."
"Please come again," he says smiling.
I step out of the shop.
Now the heavy monsoon season is going to start soon.
I now have a good raincoat and a cotton shirt.
I am now fully ready for this changing season.
I set off towards home happily.
